meta {
  name: 162. Partial charge with the static token passes auth (stale expectedDueAmount, so 409 and no money moves)
  type: http
  seq: 162
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{subRevampTorgId}}/billings/{{subRevampBillingId}}/partial-charge
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{subRevampStaticToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "mode": "TRUCKS",
    "noOfTrucks": 1,
    "createDue": true,
    "expectedDueAmount": 1.00
  }
}

assert {
  res.body.statusCode: eq 409
}

docs {
  The static VAHN_ADMIN token (zeus) may partial-charge; it used to get 403 (requireRealUser, now removed). A stale expectedDueAmount is
  rejected with 409 after auth and before anything is charged, so this proves the token got in without moving money. The real static-token
  partial charge is step 237. Needs `subRevampStaticToken` passed at run time (`--env-var`); it is never stored.
}
